Subject: [PATCH] server: PS5: a window's monitor DPI of 0 is not kept.

set_window_pos stored the monitor DPI the client sent. win32u sends 0 when it cannot find the window's monitor
(get_win_monitor_dpi of a window it cannot resolve; no monitor holds the rectangle while the display mode changes),
and the next DPI conversion of that window (map_dpi_point with a dpi of 0 falls back to it) divided by zero in
scale_dpi. On the console the server runs inside the title, so it ended every program: SIGFPE, integer divide fault,
in scale_dpi from call_req_handler, while dxgi's and d3d9ex's tests ran (B3c sweep, 2026-10-25). A DPI of 0 now keeps
the window's previous one (USER_DEFAULT_SCREEN_DPI from create_window).
---
--- a/server/window.c
+++ b/server/window.c
@@ -3206,6 +3206,11 @@
     win->paint_flags = (win->paint_flags & ~PAINT_CLIENT_FLAGS) | (req->paint_flags & PAINT_CLIENT_FLAGS);
     if (win->paint_flags & PAINT_HAS_PIXEL_FORMAT) update_pixel_format_flags( win );
 
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* A client that could not find the window's monitor sends 0; kept, it divided by zero in scale_dpi at the next
+     * DPI conversion and ended the in-title server with every program (SIGFPE, dxgi and d3d9ex tests, 2026-10-25). */
+    if (req->monitor_dpi)
+#endif
     win->monitor_dpi = req->monitor_dpi;
     old_style = win->style;
     old_window = win->window_rect;
